        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "08da1d6c-ea02-5f79-97e4-1d126abdaaca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ziggy Marley, Flea, John Frusciante, Michael Peter Balzary, Ken Chastain\n- Albums: Dragonfly, Love Is My Religion\n- Bands: Red Hot Chili Peppers, Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers\n- Roles: musician, actor, bassist, percussionist\n\nFacts:\n- After the 2000 end of Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers, Dragonfly became Ziggy Marley's first solo album, and Love Is My Religion became his second solo album.\n- On the Ziggy Marley album Dragonfly, the track \"Rainbow in the Sky\" features Flea and John Frusciante of the Red Hot Chili Peppers.\n- On the Ziggy Marley album Dragonfly, the track \"Melancholy Mood\" features only Flea.\n- Michael Peter Balzary, born on 16 October 1962 and known as Flea, is an Australian-American musician and actor.\n- Flea is best known as the bassist and a founding member of the rock band Red Hot Chili Peppers.\n- Ken Chastain performed percussion on Ziggy Marley's album Love Is My Religion.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
